<title>USA: Republic of South Africa to set 20-yr Yankee issue.</title>
<headline>Republic of South Africa to set 20-yr Yankee issue.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Republic of South Africa is expected to tap the U.S. corporate bond market with a $400 million 20-year Yankee debt offering, syndicate sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The Baa3/BB-plus rated deal was expected to price in mid-May via lead underwriter Merrill Lynch &amp; Co Inc, the sources added.</p>
<p>Unofficial price talk on the issue was seen between 190 and 210 basis points over U.S. Treasuries, they said.</p>
<p>(( -- Nancy Leinfuss, 212-859-1675 ))</p>
</text>
